CORE
main.c
--no-assertions --datarace --unwind 4 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --symmetric-instance 2 --verbosity 9
^EXIT=6$
^SIGNAL=0$
^.*refusing to continue.*$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
This program has no symmetric array family, so --symmetric-instance 2 cannot be
applied. cbmc must produce no verdict at all rather than fall back to the
unreduced program.

The reason is that the flag never travels alone: it is set in the competition
tuning table only alongside an --unwind chosen for the reduced program. On the
unreduced program that bound cuts the setup loop rather than completing it, the
unwinding assumption prunes every path, and the run reports success having
generated nothing to check -- a wrong answer on a task whose expected verdict
is false, and one scored far worse than the timeout it would replace.

So both verdict lines are forbidden here, not just the wrong one: the failure
has to be an exit with a diagnostic, and EXIT=6 is CPROVER_EXIT_INTERNAL_ERROR.
Checking only for the absence of SUCCESSFUL would let a crash pass.
